domain StructuredSemanticAuthoringKernelDesignV1Revision5Review:
  description "Corrected independent evidence-chain review of exact D11 design candidate revision five."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether revision five closes the revision-four findings and satisfies the
    accepted design-level contract for information-gaining provider recovery without
    adding an unaccepted semantic-exactness or proof-protocol requirement.
evidence E1:
  |
    Exact review subject Seal
    69c9c98937d7d610384823ae339ea464724f6e983d8b5500d3aef6942945a240
    matches the workfile SHA256
    426470047d0e380de90624192b9db71d3f30788fa44423ed0710f9cb1e6cdba4.
evidence E2:
  |
    Revision five lines 543 through 560 makes eligibility precede admission, maps zero,
    consumed, and no-basis recovery to provider_transport_unavailable, maps otherwise-
    eligible resource admission failure to resource_exhausted with exhausted dimensions
    and accounting, and retains timeout evidence on both paths.
evidence E3:
  |
    Revision five lines 772 through 781 requires separate fixture cases and outcomes for
    zero, consumed, no-basis, resource admission, late result, and blind replay.
evidence E4:
  |
    Accepted foundation revision three F8 lines 210 through 228 permits source-supported
    synthesis, creative completion, coherent interpretation, low-importance adjustment,
    valid deferral, and preserved retirement as reviewable semantic-migration outcomes
    when domain invariants hold.
evidence E5:
  |
    Accepted foundation revision three F9 lines 232 through 255 separately requires every
    retry to add information, narrow the problem, or test a materially different
    alternative; forbids blind retry; and permits repetition after transport conditions
    change. Lines 375 through 378 say execution safeguards constrain runaway execution,
    not permitted synthesis, and leave detector details to successor design and tests.
evidence E6:
  |
    Revision five lines 531 through 557 requires the server to establish exactly one
    truthful typed recoveryBasis before paid admission, disallows a model assertion as
    the basis, rejects recovery when no truthful basis exists, and assigns a distinct
    request identity to an admitted recovery.
evidence E7:
  |
    Accepted ADR0031 D11 requires exact typed DTO and patch schemas, execution-policy
    numbers, detector and window rules, public mapping, persistence and fence changes,
    adapter conformance, and controlled-port source-based retry tests. It does not state
    that design acceptance requires a general formal proof algebra for semantic
    materiality or the additional evidence subtypes proposed by the original review.
evidence E8:
  |
    The original revision-five review P1 required a server-owned materiality verifier,
    exact admissible evidence semantics, post-timeout route binding, canonical digest
    scope, and extra metadata-only and stale-evidence fixtures as design-acceptance
    blockers.
evidence E9:
  |
    After the migration and retry requirements were independently rechecked, the product
    owner instructed revision of this review under the corrected distinction. This
    instruction authorizes correction of the review record but is not evidence for the
    technical interpretation and does not accept the design.
premise C1:
  |
    Semantic-migration output exactness and retry admission are different concerns.
    Classified generative migration can coexist with strict target schema, protected
    domain invariants, reconciliation, and bounded execution controls.
premise C2:
  |
    Unequal digests alone do not prove material information gain, but that observation
    identifies a possible implementation hazard rather than a current design
    contradiction when the design already requires a truthful server-owned basis,
    rejects its absence, and requires no-blind-replay conformance evidence.
premise C3:
  |
    Turning that possible implementation hazard into a new exact proof protocol and a
    current P1 blocker adds a control not established by the accepted requirement or a
    concrete unresolved design outcome. This is AP007 Control Accretion.
premise U1:
  |
    Runtime implementation conformance, provider behavior, and the implementation's
    actual treatment of incidental digest drift remain unverified and outside this
    design review.
decision D1 based_on P1, E2, E3:
  |
    Revision five closes both revision-four P1 findings: failure classification,
    no-basis terminalization, retained receipt and matching fixture expectations are now
    explicit.
decision D2 based_on P1, E4, E5, E6, E7, E8, C1, C2, C3:
  |
    Do not adopt the original revision-five P1 finding. Its requested verifier and
    evidence protocol may be considered during implementation, but current evidence does
    not make them design-acceptance requirements. The finding confused permitted
    generative migration semantics with the separate behavioral prohibition on blind
    retry and promoted an optional elaboration into a blocker.
decision D3 based_on P1, D1, D2, E9, U1:
  |
    Report PASS for exact revision five with no P0 through P3 findings. Preserve runtime
    F9 conformance as an implementation verification obligation. Do not infer design
    acceptance, implementation, provider execution, PERT resumption, route cutover,
    deployment, production effects, pointer or policy activation, rollback, or release.
